<title>USA: N.Y. Fed Press Briefing - November 21.</title>
<headline>N.Y. Fed Press Briefing - November 21.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve had no large one-day net misses in its reserve projections in the latest week, a Fed spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The high in natural float was a bit under $2.7 billion on Thursday, while the low was a bit over $400 million on Friday.</p>
<p>Transportation float averaged about $175 million per day, with the high on Wednesday at a bit over $550 million primarily due to aircraft mechanical problems in New York and weather-related delays in Oklahoma and Seattle.</p>
<p>The New York Fed said it has discontinued the release of adjustment borrowing details as of Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Caryn Trokie, 212-859-1678</p>
